# Rust standards (CodeBrain)

Full text: `docs/agent/CODING_STANDARDS.md` · examples: `docs/agent/RUST_PRACTICES.md`

## Crates & modules

- One subsystem/responsibility per workspace crate; no business logic in CLI
- Modules are isolated by capability, private by default, and re-export stable contracts from `lib.rs`
- No `utils`/`common` god crates, cyclic dependencies, global mutable state, or duplicated DTOs
- Every crate must be independently testable (`cargo test -p <crate>`)
- Inject trait implementations at I/O/storage boundaries for testability

## Errors — no panic

- Libs: `thiserror` + `Result`. Edges: `anyhow` + `context`
- **Forbid** in non-test code: `unwrap` / `expect` / `panic!` / `todo!` / `unimplemented!` / `unreachable!`
- Prefer `get` over indexing; stubs use `bail!("… Phase N")`
- Logging: `tracing` only (no `println!` in libs)

## Traits

- Vary behavior with traits (`Connector`, future `Embedder`)
- Small traits; generics/static dispatch in hot paths; `dyn` at plugin boundaries
- `async_trait` on public async traits; bounds: `Send + Sync` where shared

## Async & concurrency

- Tokio only — never block runtime (`tokio::fs` / `spawn_blocking`)
- No `std::sync::Mutex` across `.await` — use `tokio::sync::*`
- Bound work with `Semaphore` / batching; queues via `mpsc`

## Memory

- Borrow at boundaries (`&str`, `&[u8]`); own at edges
- No clones in hot loops; batch I/O (`batch_size`); `with_capacity` when sized
- Do not load entire repos/vaults into memory

## Always

- `cargo fmt` + clippy deny (see `validate.sh`)
- Crate boundaries in `CODING_STANDARDS.md`
